      "math_academy_id": "e-1520",
      "problem": "Find the $\\textrm{GCF}$ of $9a$, $18a,$ and $27a.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $9$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 3,\\quad 9.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $18$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 2,\\quad 3,\\quad 6,\\quad 9,\\quad 18.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $27$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 3,\\quad 9,\\quad 27.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $9,$ $18,$ and $27$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 3,\\quad 9.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $9.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. The expressions $9a,$ $18a,$ and $27a$ all contain $a.$\n\nThus, the $\\textrm{GCF}$ of $9a,$ $18a,$ and $27a$ is $9a.$",
